IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `qsa-dates`
IMPORT `qsa-rules`
IMPORT `qsa-seat`

-- Succession Act 1981 (Qld) -- worked cases for the claimant's questions (qsa-seat.l4), the date helpers (qsa-dates.l4)
-- and the time-limit rule (qsa-rules.l4). Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited text; none was
-- copied from the encoding's output. Each assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law.
-- The facts are illustrative.
-- UNOFFICIAL. Based on content from the Queensland Legislation website at 6 November 2026 (c) The State of Queensland,
-- CC BY 4.0. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `cases`

`d` MEANS `the calendar date`
`any day` MEANS `d` 1 1 2000
`never` MEANS `my parent was never the deceased's spouse`

§§ `Dates: months after a day (fork F1)`
#ASSERT `the day` 6 `months after` (`d` 31 8 2025) EQUALS `d` 28 2 2026
#ASSERT `the day` 9 `months after` (`d` 31 5 2024) EQUALS `d` 28 2 2025
#ASSERT `the day` 3 `months after` (`d` 30 11 2023) EQUALS `d` 29 2 2024
#ASSERT `the day` 12 `months after` (`d` 15 3 2025) EQUALS `d` 15 3 2026
#ASSERT `the day` 1 `months after` (`d` 31 1 2025) EQUALS `d` 28 2 2025
#ASSERT `the day` 3 `months after` (`d` 15 10 2025) EQUALS `d` 15 1 2026
#ASSERT `the day` 27 `months after` (`d` 10 1 2026) EQUALS `d` 10 4 2028
-- The time-limit rule: on the last day in time, the day after not.
#ASSERT `a step on` (`d` 15 1 2026) `is in time for the last day` (`d` 15 1 2026)
#ASSERT (NOT (`a step on` (`d` 16 1 2026) `is in time for the last day` (`d` 15 1 2026)))
#ASSERT `a step on` (`d` 1 12 2025) `is in time for the last day` (`d` 15 1 2026)

